<p>(a) Earnings per share is based upon 8,736,514 and 8,527,765 weighted average shares outstanding for the quarters ended March 1997 and March 1996 respectively, and 8,688,582 weighted average shares outstanding for the quarter ended December 1996.  (The number of shares considered outstanding does not include 77,154 shares, 351,899 shares and 173,647 shares held by the Employee Stock Ownership Plan Trust at March 30, 1997, March 31, 1996 and December 29, 1996, respectively.  In accordance with generally accepted accounting principles, shares held by the Trust are not considered outstanding for earnings per share calculations until the shares are committed for release from the Trust.)</p>
